# Contributing

Thanks for considering contributing to TrueAegis.

## Good Contributions

Helpful contributions include:

- bug fixes
- documentation improvements
- validator modules
- safer detection logic
- UI improvements
- knowledge base additions
- test data
- report formatting improvements

## Rules

Please keep contributions aligned with the project goal:

> local exposure intelligence and defensive infrastructure analysis

Avoid adding:

- exploit automation
- destructive actions
- credential attacks
- stealth functionality
- unauthorized access features

## Development Setup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/TrueAegis.git
cd TrueAegis
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Pull Request Checklist

Before opening a pull request:

- [ ] code runs locally
- [ ] no credentials or private scan data included
- [ ] README updated if behavior changed
- [ ] safe/authorized use assumptions preserved
- [ ] no unnecessary dependencies added
